# Citation File Format — https://citation-file-format.github.io/
#
# GitHub reads this file and offers "Cite this repository" (APA + BibTeX) on the
# repository page. It ships inside the release zip as well: the moment someone
# needs the citation is usually the moment they are looking at the installed
# theme, not at GitHub.
#
# `version` and `date-released` are checked against config/theme.ini and
# package.json by `npm run lint:ini` — a citation that names a version the
# theme never shipped is worse than one that names none.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Africa Multiple — DRE: an Omeka S theme for the Digital Research Environment"
message: "If you use this theme, or its design system, please cite it as below."
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Madore
    given-names: Frédérick
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0959-2092"
    affiliation: "University of Bayreuth"

abstract: >-
  An Omeka S theme for the Africa Multiple Cluster of Excellence (University of
  Bayreuth), built for the Cluster's Digital Research Environment and the AMIRA
  research archive. It implements a "Scholarly Modernism" design system on an
  OKLCH design-token foundation: a single brand seed from which every accent,
  hover, focus ring and tint is derived by colour-mixing; first-class light and
  dark modes; WCAG AA contrast asserted by the build rather than by hand; and a
  record layer that renders item metadata in named scholarly groups with
  citation, DOI, permalink and licence in a sticky rail. The token layer is a
  published contract, consumed by name by the Cluster's DRE Search and
  ResourceVisualizations modules.

version: 2.29.0
date-released: "2026-08-05"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later

repository-code: "https://github.com/AM-Digital-Research-Environment/DRE-theme"
url: "https://data.africamultiple.uni-bayreuth.de/s/amira"

keywords:
  - Omeka S
  - theme
  - design system
  - design tokens
  - OKLCH
  - accessibility
  - dark mode
  - digital humanities
  - research data
  - Africa

references:
  - type: software
    title: "Lively"
    notes: >-
      The theme began in 2026 as a fork of Lively and keeps its GPLv3 licence.
      It has since been rebuilt top to bottom and is developed, versioned and
      released independently; it is not affiliated with or supported by the
      Omeka Team.
    authors:
      - name: "Omeka Team"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/omeka-s-themes/lively"
    license: GPL-3.0-or-later
